  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "NPER uses exact rate == 0 for linear branch (#DIV/0! when 1 + rate rounds to 1) and x87-stored logs elsewhere",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20131 through 16.0.20527, NPER(rate, pmt, pv, [fv], [type]) takes the linear branch -(fv + pv) / pmt only at exact rate == 0.0 (returning #DIV/0! if pmt == 0). Any nonzero rate enters the logarithmic formula using x87 PC64-to-PC53 double-rounded operations and x87 FYL2X logarithms: tiny rates where 1 + rate rounds to 1 return #DIV/0! (such as rate = 1e-300), while small rates like 1e-10 lose accuracy in LN(1 + rate). All 2,509 full-bank NPER rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0.20131, 20430, and 20527.20088, matching 2,509/2,509 full-bank and 120/120 pinned NPER rows.",
